  "text": "Classic Neapolitan ice cream features three distinct flavors layered together: lemon, chocolate, and vanilla. Here's a simple recipe:\n\n1. For vanilla: Whisk egg yolks with sugar. Cook over medium heat until thick, then add cream and let cool.\n2. For chocolate: Melt dark chocolate, mix with heavy cream, and chill.\n3. For lemon: Whisk eggs with sugar and lemon juice, cook over medium heat, then add cream and chill.\n4. Layer each flavor into a pint jar, swirl with a knife, and freeze. Enjoy your Neapolitan ice cream!",
